{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtTQ8TfrJgVLh2u1PHcj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't measure the exact token count here: there's no tokenizer installed, and the API is off-limits for this. The log gives a rough bound, though. The cached prefix today (tools plus system, with core tools) is about 1,024–1,100 tokens, and the athlete context is roughly 80–100 tokens of that. So the static instructions alone are probably around 850–950 tokens, which may be below the 1024-token minimum. I'll record that as an open risk rather than pad the prompt blind. I'll also update the README sentence that describes caching so it matches the new structure."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1669,"cache_read_input_tokens":38399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1669},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b92da95e-964e-4d04-a7f5-c03c15d988b4","uuid":"6daf4e57-f67f-4a8d-90ed-c541cab9aa85","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:26:33.319Z","request_id":"req_011CgtTQ8HGGvdzYEDnXRAws"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtTQ8TfrJgVLh2u1PHcj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R8Lzn6nN1x5me7thzHHRQp","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-YbzoOM/README.md","old_string":"Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","new_string":"Prompt caching is on: the static coaching\ninstructions are the first system block and carry the `cache_control` marker, so\ntool-loop rounds and follow-up messages inside the 5-minute window read them from\ncache. The per-athlete block (zones, goal, facts, date) is a second, uncached system\nblock, so a `save_fact` write does not evict the instructions."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1669,"cache_read_input_tokens":38399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1669},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b92da95e-964e-4d04-a7f5-c03c15d988b4","uuid":"dcd0cdf4-3838-4b81-97fb-4cfa1e5fe2f4","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:26:34.244Z","request_id":"req_011CgtTQ8HGGvdzYEDnXRAws","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01R8Lzn6nN1x5me7thzHHRQp":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-YbzoOM/README.md","old_string":"Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","new_string":"Prompt caching is on: the static coaching\ninstructions are the first system block and carry the `cache_control` marker, so\ntool-loop rounds and follow-up messages inside the 5-minute window read them from\ncache. The per-athlete block (zones, goal, facts, date) is a second, uncached system\nblock, so a `save_fact` write does not evict the instructions."}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R8Lzn6nN1x5me7thzHHRQp","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/h-YbzoOM/README.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b92da95e-964e-4d04-a7f5-c03c15d988b4","uuid":"7144b552-b90c-40b5-bcbc-5efee8369900","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:26:34.263Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-YbzoOM/README.md","oldString":"Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","newString":"Prompt caching is on: the static coaching\ninstructions are the first system block and carry the `cache_control` marker, so\ntool-loop rounds and follow-up messages inside the 5-minute window read them from\ncache. The per-athlete block (zones, goal, facts, date) is a second, uncached system\nblock, so a `save_fact` write does not evict the instructions.","originalFile":"# pace-bot\n\nA coaching chat bot on Claude for a small running/cycling club. It is stateless\nby design: each message rebuilds the system prompt (coaching rules + the athlete's\nprofile, zones, goal and long-term facts from `data/athletes.json`), picks the tools\nthe message might need (`save_fact` and `log_session` always, planning or race tools\nwhen keywords match) and runs a short tool-use loop. `save_fact` is how the bot\nremembers durable things an athlete tells it; the next message sees the fact in\nits system prompt. Every API call appends its `usage` object to `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\nRun it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type\nmessages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs\n`COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).\nRequires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":11,"oldLines":6,"newStart":11,"newLines":8,"lines":[" Run it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type"," messages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs"," `COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).","-Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system","-prompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up","-messages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","+Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the static coaching","+instructions are the first system block and carry the `cache_control` marker, so","+tool-loop rounds and follow-up messages inside the 5-minute window read them from","+cache. The per-athlete block (zones, goal, facts, date) is a second, uncached system","+block, so a `save_fact` write does not evict the instructions."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01R8Lzn6nN1x5me7thzHHRQp","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtTR2ub7qFb1AHUt97tX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Bp5VGS4oCLqwke21p4i2bw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-YbzoOM/ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix: `save_fact` evicting the static instructions from the prompt cache\n\n## Cause\n\n`build_system()` put the coaching instructions and the per-athlete context\n(zones, goal, today's date, long-term facts) into one text block with the\n`cache_control` marker. A `save_fact` call changes the facts list, so the cached\ntext changed, and the next request missed the cache and wrote the whole prefix again.\n\n`logs/usage.jsonl` shows it: the request right after each `save_fact` has\n`cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and a fresh `cache_creation_input_tokens` of about\n1000+. The save happens in round 1, so round 2 pays the write, and the next user\nmessage pays it again.\n\n## Change (`bot.py`, `build_system`)\n\nThe system prompt is now two blocks:\n\n1. `INSTRUCTIONS`, identical for every athlete and every day, with\n   `cache_control: ephemeral`. This is the cached prefix.\n2. `athlete_context(a, today)`, no cache marker. It holds the facts, zones, goal\n   and date, which are the parts that change.\n\nA `save_fact` now changes only block 2, and block 1 still reads from cache. The\ndate moved into block 2 too, so the instructions no longer change at midnight.\n\n`README.md`: the caching paragraph now describes the two-block layout.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `scratch/check_cache.py` (outside the repo, in `/tmp/h-YbzoOM/scratch/`) runs\n  `reply()` through a fake LLM with a `save_fact` turn. It redirects the athlete and\n  usage files to scratch, so `data/` and `logs/` are untouched. It checks that:\n  - block 1 has the cache marker and is byte-identical across all calls, including\n    the ones before and after the save;\n  - block 2 is not cached;\n  - the saved fact appears in block 2 of the next request, and not in block 1.\n  Result: all checks pass.\n- I did not call the Anthropic API, so this does not show real cache hits.\n\n## Open risk: the cached prefix may be under the minimum\n\nCaching only applies when the cached prefix is at least 1024 tokens for Sonnet-class\nmodels (please check the current docs). Below that, the marker is silently ignored.\nBefore this change, the prefix was tools + instructions + athlete context. The log\nshows it at about 1024–1100 tokens with core tools, so it was just over the minimum.\n\nAfter this change the cached prefix is tools + instructions only. My rough estimate\nis about 850–950 tokens for the instructions plus core tools, which may be under\n1024. If so, caching would stop working on every call, not only after `save_fact`.\nI could not measure the exact count: there is no local tokenizer, and I did not call\nthe API.\n\nHow to check after a deploy: the first call of a conversation should show\n`cache_creation_input_tokens > 0`, and the next call `cache_read_input_tokens > 0`.\nIf both stay at 0, the instructions are under the minimum. The fix then needs about\n150–300 more tokens of stable content in `INSTRUCTIONS`, or fewer requests with\nthe tool-group variants (see below). I did not pad the prompt, since that changes\nthe bot's behaviour and I cannot measure the gap.\n\n## Not changed: tool sets split the cache\n\n`select_tools()` adds the `plan` and `race` tools on keyword match. The tool list\ncomes before the system prompt in the cached prefix, so each distinct tool set has\nits own cache entry. A message with \"plan\" in it will write its own prefix rather\nthan read the core-tools entry. The log shows this (`plan_week` calls write about\n1305 tokens). This predates the change and is separate from the `save_fact` problem.\nIf the prefix-size risk above is real, always sending the full tool list would be\nthe simplest way to get one cache entry. That trades away the March keyword-filter\nsaving, so I left it for you to decide.\n\n## Files\n\n- `bot.py`: `build_system()` returns two blocks.\n- `README.md`: the caching paragraph.\n- `ANSWER.md`: this file.\n- Not committed.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2202,"cache_read_input_tokens":40068,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2202},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b92da95e-964e-4d04-a7f5-c03c15d988b4","uuid":"d067ab0e-dc51-4e73-a9dd-1956b7344ad3","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:26:41.926Z","request_id":"req_011CgtTR2ivfXKj58gfHZ7A8","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Bp5VGS4oCLqwke21p4i2bw":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-YbzoOM/ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix: `save_fact` evicting the static instructions from the prompt cache\n\n## Cause\n\n`build_system()` put the coaching instructions and the per-athlete context\n(zones, goal, today's date, long-term facts) into one text block with the\n`cache_control` marker. A `save_fact` call changes the facts list, so the cached\ntext changed, and the next request missed the cache and wrote the whole prefix again.\n\n`logs/usage.jsonl` shows it: the request right after each `save_fact` has\n`cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and a fresh `cache_creation_input_tokens` of about\n1000+. The save happens in round 1, so round 2 pays the write, and the next user\nmessage pays it again.\n\n## Change (`bot.py`, `build_system`)\n\nThe system prompt is now two blocks:\n\n1. `INSTRUCTIONS`, identical for every athlete and every day, with\n   `cache_control: ephemeral`. This is the cached prefix.\n2. `athlete_context(a, today)`, no cache marker. It holds the facts, zones, goal\n   and date, which are the parts that change.\n\nA `save_fact` now changes only block 2, and block 1 still reads from cache. The\ndate moved into block 2 too, so the instructions no longer change at midnight.\n\n`README.md`: the caching paragraph now describes the two-block layout.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `scratch/check_cache.py` (outside the repo, in `/tmp/h-YbzoOM/scratch/`) runs\n  `reply()` through a fake LLM with a `save_fact` turn. It redirects the athlete and\n  usage files to scratch, so `data/` and `logs/` are untouched. It checks that:\n  - block 1 has the cache marker and is byte-identical across all calls, including\n    the ones before and after the save;\n  - block 2 is not cached;\n  - the saved fact appears in block 2 of the next request, and not in block 1.\n  Result: all checks pass.\n- I did not call the Anthropic API, so this does not show real cache hits.\n\n## Open risk: the cached prefix may be under the minimum\n\nCaching only applies when the cached prefix is at least 1024 tokens for Sonnet-class\nmodels (please check the current docs). Below that, the marker is silently ignored.\nBefore this change, the prefix was tools + instructions + athlete context. The log\nshows it at about 1024–1100 tokens with core tools, so it was just over the minimum.\n\nAfter this change the cached prefix is tools + instructions only. My rough estimate\nis about 850–950 tokens for the instructions plus core tools, which may be under\n1024. If so, caching would stop working on every call, not only after `save_fact`.\nI could not measure the exact count: there is no local tokenizer, and I did not call\nthe API.\n\nHow to check after a deploy: the first call of a conversation should show\n`cache_creation_input_tokens > 0`, and the next call `cache_read_input_tokens > 0`.\nIf both stay at 0, the instructions are under the minimum. The fix then needs about\n150–300 more tokens of stable content in `INSTRUCTIONS`, or fewer requests with\nthe tool-group variants (see below). I did not pad the prompt, since that changes\nthe bot's behaviour and I cannot measure the gap.\n\n## Not changed: tool sets split the cache\n\n`select_tools()` adds the `plan` and `race` tools on keyword match. The tool list\ncomes before the system prompt in the cached prefix, so each distinct tool set has\nits own cache entry. A message with \"plan\" in it will write its own prefix rather\nthan read the core-tools entry. The log shows this (`plan_week` calls write about\n1305 tokens). This predates the change and is separate from the `save_fact` problem.\nIf the prefix-size risk above is real, always sending the full tool list would be\nthe simplest way to get one cache entry. That trades away the March keyword-filter\nsaving, so I left it for you to decide.\n\n## Files\n\n- `bot.py`: `build_system()` returns two blocks.\n- `README.md`: the caching paragraph.\n- `ANSWER.md`: this file.\n- Not committed.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bp5VGS4oCLqwke21p4i2bw","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /private/tmp/h-YbzoOM/ANSWER.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b92da95e-964e-4d04-a7f5-c03c15d988b4","uuid":"02523f2a-bf1b-44cb-a12d-1774bba46b3c","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:26:41.936Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/private/tmp/h-YbzoOM/ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix: `save_fact` evicting the static instructions from the prompt cache\n\n## Cause\n\n`build_system()` put the coaching instructions and the per-athlete context\n(zones, goal, today's date, long-term facts) into one text block with the\n`cache_control` marker. A `save_fact` call changes the facts list, so the cached\ntext changed, and the next request missed the cache and wrote the whole prefix again.\n\n`logs/usage.jsonl` shows it: the request right after each `save_fact` has\n`cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and a fresh `cache_creation_input_tokens` of about\n1000+. The save happens in round 1, so round 2 pays the write, and the next user\nmessage pays it again.\n\n## Change (`bot.py`, `build_system`)\n\nThe system prompt is now two blocks:\n\n1. `INSTRUCTIONS`, identical for every athlete and every day, with\n   `cache_control: ephemeral`. This is the cached prefix.\n2. `athlete_context(a, today)`, no cache marker. It holds the facts, zones, goal\n   and date, which are the parts that change.\n\nA `save_fact` now changes only block 2, and block 1 still reads from cache. The\ndate moved into block 2 too, so the instructions no longer change at midnight.\n\n`README.md`: the caching paragraph now describes the two-block layout.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `scratch/check_cache.py` (outside the repo, in `/tmp/h-YbzoOM/scratch/`) runs\n  `reply()` through a fake LLM with a `save_fact` turn. It redirects the athlete and\n  usage files to scratch, so `data/` and `logs/` are untouched. It checks that:\n  - block 1 has the cache marker and is byte-identical across all calls, including\n    the ones before and after the save;\n  - block 2 is not cached;\n  - the saved fact appears in block 2 of the next request, and not in block 1.\n  Result: all checks pass.\n- I did not call the Anthropic API, so this does not show real cache hits.\n\n## Open risk: the cached prefix may be under the minimum\n\nCaching only applies when the cached prefix is at least 1024 tokens for Sonnet-class\nmodels (please check the current docs). Below that, the marker is silently ignored.\nBefore this change, the prefix was tools + instructions + athlete context. The log\nshows it at about 1024–1100 tokens with core tools, so it was just over the minimum.\n\nAfter this change the cached prefix is tools + instructions only. My rough estimate\nis about 850–950 tokens for the instructions plus core tools, which may be under\n1024. If so, caching would stop working on every call, not only after `save_fact`.\nI could not measure the exact count: there is no local tokenizer, and I did not call\nthe API.\n\nHow to check after a deploy: the first call of a conversation should show\n`cache_creation_input_tokens > 0`, and the next call `cache_read_input_tokens > 0`.\nIf both stay at 0, the instructions are under the minimum. The fix then needs about\n150–300 more tokens of stable content in `INSTRUCTIONS`, or fewer requests with\nthe tool-group variants (see below). I did not pad the prompt, since that changes\nthe bot's behaviour and I cannot measure the gap.\n\n## Not changed: tool sets split the cache\n\n`select_tools()` adds the `plan` and `race` tools on keyword match. The tool list\ncomes before the system prompt in the cached prefix, so each distinct tool set has\nits own cache entry. A message with \"plan\" in it will write its own prefix rather\nthan read the core-tools entry. The log shows this (`plan_week` calls write about\n1305 tokens). This predates the change and is separate from the `save_fact` problem.\nIf the prefix-size risk above is real, always sending the full tool list would be\nthe simplest way to get one cache entry. That trades away the March keyword-filter\nsaving, so I left it for you to decide.\n\n## Files\n\n- `bot.py`: `build_system()` returns two blocks.\n- `README.md`: the caching paragraph.\n- `ANSWER.md`: this file.\n- Not committed.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Bp5VGS4oCLqwke21p4i2bw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
