{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XUT6UyzZVB7Fa6uThvKoR9","type":"tool_result","content":" M README.md\n M bot.py\n?? ANSWER.md\n?? scratch/\ndiff --git a/bot.py b/bot.py\nindex e2ff241..4ae623d 100644\n--- a/bot.py\n+++ b/bot.py\n@@ -128,9 +128,14 @@ def athlete_context(a, today):\n \n \n def build_system(a, today):\n-    # One block, cached as a whole: instructions + per-athlete context.\n-    text = INSTRUCTIONS + \"\\n\\n\" + athlete_context(a, today)\n-    return [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}]\n+    # Two blocks. The first is identical for every athlete and every day, so it is\n+    # the cached prefix. The per-athlete block (facts, zones, date) comes after the\n+    # breakpoint and is not cached: a save_fact changes only this block, and the\n+    # static instructions keep their cache entry.\n+    return [\n+        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n+        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today)},\n+    ]\n \n # --------------------------------------------------------------------------- tools\n CORE_TOOLS = [\nCOMPILES","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b92da95e-964e-4d04-a7f5-c03c15d988b4","uuid":"2feb9eba-a400-446a-8d57-26f57c2c5c6e","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:26:43.979Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":" M README.md\n M bot.py\n?? ANSWER.md\n?? scratch/\ndiff --git a/bot.py b/bot.py\nindex e2ff241..4ae623d 100644\n--- a/bot.py\n+++ b/bot.py\n@@ -128,9 +128,14 @@ def athlete_context(a, today):\n \n \n def build_system(a, today):\n-    # One block, cached as a whole: instructions + per-athlete context.\n-    text = INSTRUCTIONS + \"\\n\\n\" + athlete_context(a, today)\n-    return [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}]\n+    # Two blocks. The first is identical for every athlete and every day, so it is\n+    # the cached prefix. The per-athlete block (facts, zones, date) comes after the\n+    # breakpoint and is not cached: a save_fact changes only this block, and the\n+    # static instructions keep their cache entry.\n+    return [\n+        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n+        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today)},\n+    ]\n \n # --------------------------------------------------------------------------- tools\n CORE_TOOLS = [\nCOMPILES","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XUT6UyzZVB7Fa6uThvKoR9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtTRkKiYq8QCQNdccULY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I split the system prompt so a `save_fact` no longer evicts the static instructions from the cache. A fake-LLM check passes, but I couldn't confirm real cache hits. There's also a risk that caching now switches off entirely, which I haven't ruled out.\n\n**Cause:** `build_system()` put the instructions and the per-athlete facts into one cached block. Each `save_fact` changed that block, so the next request rewrote the whole prefix. The log shows it: the request after each save has `cache_read_input_tokens: 0`.\n\n**Change (`bot.py`):** the system prompt is now two blocks.\n- The instructions come first, identical for every athlete and day, with the cache marker.\n- The athlete context (zones, goal, date, facts) follows, uncached.\n\nI also moved the date into the uncached block, so the instructions no longer change at midnight. The caching paragraph in `README.md` now describes the new layout.\n\n**Verification:** `/tmp/h-YbzoOM/scratch/check_cache.py` runs `reply()` through a fake LLM with a save turn. It checks that the cached block is byte-identical across calls and that the saved fact reaches the next request. All checks pass. It redirects the data and log files to scratch, so `data/` and `logs/` are untouched. I did not call the API.\n\n**Open risk:** caching only applies above a minimum prefix length (1024 tokens for Sonnet-class models, per my understanding of the docs). The cached prefix is now tools plus instructions only. My rough estimate puts that at about 850–950 tokens, which may be under the minimum. If it is, caching would stop on every call, not just after saves. I couldn't measure the exact count here. After a deploy, check that `cache_creation_input_tokens` is above 0 on the first call and `cache_read_input_tokens` is above 0 on the next. If both stay at 0, the instructions need roughly 150–300 more tokens of stable content. I didn't pad the prompt blind, because that changes the bot's behaviour.\n\n`ANSWER.md` has the full write-up, including a note that the keyword tool groups split the cache by tool set. That predates this change and I left it alone. Nothing is committed, and nothing was deployed or sent anywhere external."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":605,"cache_read_input_tokens":43791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":605},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b92da95e-964e-4d04-a7f5-c03c15d988b4","uuid":"889248bd-2a27-4c9a-81ed-ba368f1143d4","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:26:48.454Z","request_id":"req_011CgtTRkA3PdD9r9uuYv1Yz"}
